The three of us sit around the table.
First, I serve them rice.
After that, I take the chicken curry.
Kiran asks, "Maya, shall I take some curry?"
I say, "Certainly, pour two spoons of curry first."
Then Sara also takes the curry.
We start eating the food together.
Sara eats a little curry.
She says happily, "Maya, this is very tasty!"
Kiran also agrees.
He says, "Yes, this has the taste of an authentic Kerala curry."
I thank them.
I feel very happy.
They eat more rice and curry.
We talk about the badminton game.
The sound of the rain can still be heard outside.
This Sunday lunch is a very good experience.
